**Solution:** `CustomerEscalationTriage/CustomerEscalationTriage.uipx`

### Flow topology

```
Manual Trigger → Classify Escalation (Script) → End
```

### Inputs (5)
| Variable | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `customerTier` | string | `Enterprise`, `Pro`, `Standard`, `Free` |
| `productionDown` | boolean | Whether production is down |
| `workaroundAvailable` | boolean | Whether a workaround exists |
| `businessImpact` | string | `High`, `Medium`, `Low` |
| `correlationId` | string | Correlation identifier |

### Outputs (4)
| Variable | Type | Values |
|---|---|---|
| `severity` | string | `Sev1` / `Sev2` / `Sev3` / `Sev4` |
| `engineeringNeeded` | boolean | `true` for Sev1 or Sev2 |
| `responseMode` | string | `Immediate` / `Urgent` / `SLA-bound` / `Best-effort` |
| `caseKey` | string | `{correlationId}-{severity}` |

### Classification logic
| Condition | Severity |
|---|---|
| Production down **AND** no workaround **AND** (Enterprise or High impact) | **Sev1** → Immediate, engineering required |
| Production down **AND** (workaround exists OR Pro tier OR High impact) | **Sev2** → Urgent, engineering required |
| Medium impact OR Enterprise OR Pro tier (no prod-down) | **Sev3** → SLA-bound |
| Everything else | **Sev4** → Best-effort |

